# Feature Catalog

Use this rule when locating an existing feature or adding a course-level capability.

## Product areas

- Course setup and content: `src/routes/route-mongo.ts`, `src/db/mongo/course-mongo.ts`, instructor onboarding and Documents UI.
- Student learning assistant: chat modes, RAG course materials, flags, and memory-agent struggle topics.
- Instructor operations: Documents, Monitor, Flags, prompts, reports, and course information.
- Writing Feedback: optional instructor/TA assessment workspace under `src/writing-feedback/` and `.cursor/rules/writing-feedback/`.

## Optional capability convention

- Persist capability configuration on `activeCourse.features`; missing values mean disabled.
- Default new capabilities to disabled for backward compatibility.
- Hide disabled UI and enforce the same gate server-side; UI hiding is never authorization.
- Only instructors/admins change course capabilities. Course staff may operate enabled capabilities according to their role.
- Disabling a capability preserves records and audit history unless a separately approved deletion workflow exists.
- Document the capability endpoint, type change, migration/default behavior, and navigation entry.
